The cron full-suite gate has been RED since 2026-08-11 with three
failures. Topping up the test-agent-infra install list was refused twice
as guesswork, and rightly: the container had hypergumbo_core importable
while rich -- a declared dependency of that very package -- was absent,
which the workflow file cannot produce. The leading explanation was a
shared site-packages volume carrying a stale editable install, and under
that explanation adding names to the pip line turns the gate green while
it silently tests an OLD tree. Worse than the red, because it is quiet.

That explanation is now dead, by reproduction rather than argument. In a
clean venv carrying exactly the four packages that step installs:

  pytest tests/                               ->  2 failed
  pytest tests/test_rct_public_api_pinned.py  ->  8 failed

Same tree, same interpreter. Fourteen scripts/check-* and generate-*
helpers do sys.path.insert(0, .../hypergumbo-core/src) at module level,
and sibling tests exec them through SourceFileLoader. The insert lands
in the shared interpreter, so whether the pinning tests could import
anything came down to which other tests shared their xdist worker.
Nothing was stale. The earlier "8 of 9 fail locally, 2 in CI"
discrepancy was an artifact of running that file ALONE.

  * the module declares the one source root it needs, so it behaves the
    same run alone as in the suite;
  * a guard re-runs it in a child interpreter with the in-repo package
    roots scrubbed. That subprocess is not ceremony -- on a dev box the
    editable install makes those imports succeed no matter what, so an
    in-process assertion would pass with or without the fix;
  * rich and mypy join the install list for what actually needs them:
    cli.py imports rich at module scope, and the mypy-gate test's
    positive control asserts the ratchet's exit 1 (regression), which it
    cannot reach at exit 2 (its documented infra failure with mypy
    absent). Verified in the same venv: with mypy present the ratchet
    returns 1 and reports REGRESSION.

Controls: the guard passes with the declaration and fails without it.
CI-equivalent rerun of the whole step: 1518 passed, 0 failed.

